& [IR3OperatorHarnessImplementationPlanV1] is the IR3-S04 plan for bounded operator harness implementation activation
  + [plan_id] is ir3-operator-harness-implementation-plan-v1
  + [plan_uuid] is 9f943b75-4ea6-4b15-a63d-40afa4425314
  + [slice_id] is IR3-S04
  + [plan_status] is accepted_by_completion_review_pending
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [implementation_scope] is implementation file inventory and activation plan only

  = must: define future implementation files, public API boundaries, generated trace writer boundaries, fixture runner boundaries, command plan, dependency boundary, and proof checklist
  = must: preserve that actual code creation remains gated until a later activation pack or implementation slice accepts it
  = must: keep all future implementation side effects inside accepted generated output roots
  - never: write operator harness code, fixture source, expected ledgers, generated traces, tests, dependencies, operations control, or live machine control in this slice

& [ImplementationFileInventory: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future file inventory for bounded IR3 implementation
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/operators/contracts.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is define frozen dataclasses and validation helpers for operator contracts, operator requests, operator results, refusals, faults, and trace event envelopes
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/operators/runner.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is evaluate contract-driven operator requests against accepted contracts, input refs, safety limits, refusal rules, and fault rules without live dispatch
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/operators/traces.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is build non-authoritative trace events, non-authority warnings, deterministic trace identities, generated output manifests, and stale trace markers
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/operators/fixture_runner.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is load tracked fixture source and expected ledgers, run accepted in-process operator functions, write generated traces only under accepted roots, and compare trace facts to expected ledgers
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/operators/__init__.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is expose only bounded operator harness APIs after implementation activation and keep live-control names absent
  + [future_test_file] is tests/test_ir3_operator_harness_contracts.py
  + [future_test_file_role] is contract tests over runner request validation, refusal/fault outcomes, trace identity, generated path refusal, non-authority warnings, and no live-control API exposure

  = must: treat this file inventory as the maximum implementation candidate set until IR3 completion review or a future rebake changes it
  = must: require deeper reasoning review before creating or editing files outside this inventory for IR3 operator harness implementation
  = must: keep implementation code creation gated until a later accepted implementation activation slice opens it

& [AllowedStandardLibrarySet: IR3OperatorHarness] is the implementation dependency boundary for IR3 code
  + [allowed_stdlib] is dataclasses
  + [allowed_stdlib] is enum
  + [allowed_stdlib] is hashlib
  + [allowed_stdlib] is json
  + [allowed_stdlib] is pathlib
  + [allowed_stdlib] is typing
  + [allowed_stdlib] is unittest
  + [external_dependency_set] is empty

  = must: use Python standard library only for the first IR3 implementation pass
  = must: require a dependency-authorizing slice before adding external packages or lockfiles

& [PublicAPIBoundary: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future public API boundary for IR3 implementation
  + [api] is validate_operator_request(request, contract_index, authority_index, policy) returns validation_result, refusal, or fault
  + [api] is run_contract_operator(request, operator_function, input_records, policy) returns operator_result and operator_trace
  + [api] is build_operator_trace(request, outcome, input_refs, output_refs, trace_policy) returns non-authoritative trace event
  + [api] is validate_generated_output_path(path, generated_output_policy) returns accepted generated path or refusal
  + [api] is run_operator_fixture(fixture_case, expected_ledger, runner_policy) returns generated fixture comparison report
  + [api_status] is future implementation target only

  = must: keep APIs pure or generated-output-bounded where possible
  = must: make refusal, fault, stale, and non-authority status visible in return values
  = must: return blocked or fault reports instead of throwing away ambiguous authority material
  = must: avoid APIs named or shaped as live dispatch, job control, process control, GPU control, network control, or operations control

& [NoMutationSourceReaderPolicy: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future source-reader safety policy
  + [read_scope] is accepted docs/, accepted fixture source roots, accepted expected ledger roots, and generated projections with source lineage
  + [write_scope] is generated roots accepted by IR3-S03 only
  + [forbidden_write] is docs/**
  + [forbidden_write] is README.md
  + [forbidden_write] is pyproject.toml
  + [forbidden_write] is platform/**
  + [forbidden_write] is src/** during runtime execution
  + [forbidden_write] is tests/fixtures/sop/**
  + [forbidden_write] is tests/fixtures/expected/**
  + [forbidden_write] is tests/** during runtime execution except future test-created generated output under tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/

  = must: treat source mutation attempts as implementation faults
  = must: keep validation and trace-building side-effect-free except for explicit generated diagnostics returned to caller

& [GeneratedTraceWriterPolicy: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future generated trace writer policy
  + [allowed_write_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [allowed_write_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/traces/
  + [allowed_write_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/reports/
  + [allowed_write_root] is .langsop/traces/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [allowed_write_root] is .langsop/reports/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [allowed_write_root] is .langsop/fixtures/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [write_precondition] is operator_request validated
  + [write_precondition] is operator contract version resolved
  + [write_precondition] is authority basis and source hashes captured
  + [write_precondition] is generated output root validated inside accepted root
  + [write_precondition] is non_authority_warning present
  + [write_result] is generated projection only

  = must: refuse writes outside accepted generated roots
  = must: preserve failed runner reports without mutating SOP authority
  = must: make generated artifacts disposable and reproducible

& [FixtureRunnerImplementationBoundary] is the future fixture runner boundary for IR3 implementation
  + [allowed_fixture_source_root] is tests/fixtures/sop/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [allowed_expected_ledger_root] is tests/fixtures/expected/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [allowed_generated_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [fixture_execution_mode] is in_process_pure_operator_only
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is shell execution
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is subprocess control
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is job dispatch
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is network access
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is credential access
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is process control
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is GPU control
  + [fixture_execution_forbidden] is live machine control

  = must: compare generated traces to tracked expected ledgers without promoting traces to authority
  = must: fail closed when fixture source, expected ledger, or generated root is outside accepted policy

& [ImplementationCommandPlan: IR3OperatorHarness] is the future command and verification plan for IR3 implementation
  + [baseline_test_command] is python -m unittest discover -s tests
  + [baseline_compile_command] is python -m compileall -q src tests
  + [future_targeted_test] is python -m unittest tests.test_ir3_operator_harness_contracts
  + [diff_hygiene_command] is git diff --check
  + [fixture_policy] is tests must use tracked fixture source and expected ledgers, with generated outputs under tests/fixtures/generated/ir3_operator_harness/
  + [trace_policy] is tests may create generated trace files only under generated paths and must not track them

  = must: run baseline tests and diff hygiene after every future implementation slice
  = should: run compile check after code slices begin
  = must: run targeted contract tests once tests.test_ir3_operator_harness_contracts exists

& [ImplementationProofChecklist: IR3OperatorHarness] is the proof checklist for later code activation
  + [proof_check] is implementation files match ImplementationFileInventory: IR3OperatorHarness
  + [proof_check] is external dependency set remains empty
  + [proof_check] is operator_request validation rejects missing contract version, missing authority, undeclared output kinds, unsafe operations requests, and refusal_allowed false
  + [proof_check] is runner returns refusal or fault records instead of silent success for stale, ambiguous, unsupported, or unsafe inputs
  + [proof_check] is trace events preserve trace identity fields, source refs, generated output refs, and non-authority warnings
  + [proof_check] is generated trace writer refuses writes outside accepted generated roots
  + [proof_check] is fixture runner reads only tracked fixture source and expected ledgers and writes only generated outputs
  + [proof_check] is generated traces and reports are ignored, disposable, and reproducible
  + [proof_check] is source files, expected ledgers, and tracked SOP authority are not mutated by runtime code or tests
  + [proof_check] is operations control and live machine control remain absent

  = must: require completion review before any implementation output is accepted
  = must: fail implementation review if any proof check fails

